THOUGHT: The NullAway error is about `controller` potentially being null at `controller.detach();`. The map can contain null values, so even if the key is present, `get` may return null. I should add a null-check before dereferencing. I’ll update the method accordingly and then run the Gradle compile to ensure the error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '52,54c\      IEntityController controller = this.controllers.get(typeKey.get());
      if (controller != null) {
        controller.detach();
        this.controllers.remove(typeKey.get());
        this.animationController = null;
      }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/entities/EntityControllers.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:|error\(s\)" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

